Unreleased
----------

Cherry-picks from upstream WebRTC main on top of M145 (branch-heads/7632).

Breaking changes:

  * AudioProcessing::Config::EchoCanceller::mobile_mode is removed, and AECm
    can no longer be enabled (the AECm sources remain, unused)
  * The pipeline.multi_channel_render and pipeline.multi_channel_capture
    config defaults are now true
  * NeuralResidualEchoEstimator has a new pure virtual method, AdjustConfig()

Behaviour changes:

  * The AGC2 input volume controller's maximum target speech level is now
    -12 dBFS (was -30 dBFS)

Upstream commits, in order:

  * 8cd8620980 Remove the possibility to run AECm (prerequisite)
  * 1d1ee4503c Refactor AudioProcessingTest to match current audio processing
    code (prerequisite, tests only)
  * a6d83994aa Remove aec_mobile (AECm) config from audio_processing.h
  * 297352a2fd Update comfort noise to be applied identically on all channels
  * 573e746914 Correct the switching between the coarse and refined filters
  * 7c388cbabb Changing default values of multi channel processing to be true
  * 7f5a8b656c Propagate delay estimator fields to AecState
  * d460e60e19 AEC3: Fix render buffer headroom calculation on underruns
  * d9b92fe1bc Make max target input level for input controller -12dB
  * e10cd19640 Enable dynamic on-the-fly AEC3 configuration updates for the
    suppressor gain computation
  * fe9c0a1de4 Remove the field trial WebRTC-Aec3AecStateFullResetKillSwitch
  * 32feae39d0 Remove the field trial WebRTC-Aec3TransparentModeKillSwitch
  * 4252c6051d Remove the field trial
    WebRTC-Aec3CoarseFilterResetHangoverKillSwitch
  * 8dd6b47c83 Remove the field trial
    WebRTC-Aec3DeactivateInitialStateResetKillSwitch
  * 86ef7fa42d aec: fix wrong sentinel usage in echo metrics
  * 05d6bc269c Remove the field trial WebRTC-Aec3HighPassFilterEchoReference
  * 401392b7e6 Remove the field trial
    WebRTC-Aec3EchoSaturationDetectionKillSwitch

The ApmTest.Process reference data (output_data_float.pb) is regenerated for
the new multi-channel defaults.


Release 3.0
-----------

Bump to code from WebRTC M145 (branch-heads/7632) version.

Breaking changes:

  * C++20 is now required (previously C++17)
  * New Environment API: AudioProcessing is now created via
    BuiltinAudioProcessingBuilder and requires an Environment object
  * Namespace consolidation: Some types moved from rtc:: to webrtc:: namespace
    (ArrayView, scoped_refptr, split, etc.)

Changes include:

  * Various improvements to AEC3, AGC2, and noise suppression
  * New BuiltinAudioProcessingBuilder for creating AudioProcessing instances
  * New Environment and FieldTrials configuration system
  * Updated RNN VAD model for improved voice activity detection
  * Performance improvements across multiple platforms
  * Updated patches for BSD, MinGW, MSVC compatibility
  * Several upstream patches are now integrated (abseil-cpp 202508, gcc-15)

API migration guide:

  Before (M131):
    auto apm = webrtc::AudioProcessingBuilder()
        .SetConfig(config)
        .Create();

  After (M145):
    webrtc::Environment env = webrtc::CreateEnvironment();
    auto apm = webrtc::BuiltinAudioProcessingBuilder(config).Build(env);


Release 2.1
-----------

Build-system fixups to install more headers, add a missing absl dependency, and
forward port some missing patches to fix Windows builds.


Release 2.0
-----------

Bump to code from WebRTC M131 version.

Changes include:

  * Minor (breaking) API changes upstream
  * Various improvements to the AEC implementation
  * Transient suppression is removed
  * ExperimentalAgc and ExperimentalNs are removed
  * iSAC and the webrtc-audio-coding library were removed
  * abseil-cpp dependency bumped to 20240722
  * NEON runtime detection dropped following upstream
  * Fixes for building on i686 and MIPS
  * Support for BSDs is added
  * Other build-system cleanups
  * Patches to upstream are now also tracked in patches/


